Minimum Cost to Acquire Required Items
Problem Link: LeetCode – Minimum Cost to Acquire Required Items
Approach: Greedy / Case Analysis
We have three possible ways to acquire the required items:
1. Buy items separately: Purchase need1 items of type 1 and need2 items of type 2 individually.
2. Buy only combined items: Purchase max(need1, need2) combined items. This satisfies both requirements.
3. Buy combined + individual items: Purchase min(need1, need2) combined items to satisfy the smaller requirement, then purchase the remaining items individually.
Calculate the cost of all three possibilities and return the minimum.
Code
class Solution {
public:
    long long minimumCost(int cost1, int cost2, int costBoth, int need1, int need2) {
        long long res1 = (need1 * 1LL * cost1) + (need2 * 1LL * cost2);

        long long res2 = max(need1, need2) * 1LL * costBoth;

        long long temp = min(need1, need2) * 1LL * costBoth;

        if(need1 > need2) {
            temp += (need1 - need2) * 1LL * cost1;
        }
        else {
            temp += (need2 - need1) * 1LL * cost2;
        }

        return min({res1, res2, temp});
    }
};


Complexity Analysis
- Time Complexity: \(O(1)\) – Only a constant number of arithmetic operations and comparisons.
- Space Complexity: \(O(1)\) – No extra space is used.
Key Takeaway
Instead of exploring every possible combination, we calculate the cost of three optimal purchasing strategies and select the minimum.

This is a constant-time solution using simple greedy case analysis.
